# TODO - Implement QCA9565 Bluetooth USB support

## Owner directive

The project must implement Wi-Fi, Bluetooth and AirDrop. QCA9565/DW1707 is a
combined Wi-Fi/Bluetooth 4.0 chip, not an assumed separate Bluetooth chipset.
Shared silicon does not replace the Bluetooth USB HCI/firmware driver path.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Implement source-backed USB identity matching, HCI transport and any
      required firmware bootstrap for the target QCA9565 Bluetooth function.
      Never infer an exact USB VID/PID from the WLAN PCI ID alone.
- [ ] Research the target Tahoe Bluetooth host/USB contracts and firmware
      ROM/build matching. Use licensed firmware with correct notices; never
      substitute unrelated firmware or advertise readiness without startup.
- [ ] Integrate Bluetooth start/stop, reset, ownership, error reporting,
      sleep/resume and Wi-Fi/Bluetooth coexistence in the production target.
- [ ] Connect BLE discovery/advertising and the macOS Bluetooth stack needed
      by the required AirDrop implementation; no fabricated adapter/state.
- [ ] Verify protocol behavior with offline source-backed fixtures and record
      remaining platform assumptions. No physical log, EEPROM dump or pairing
      test is a prerequisite for completing this source implementation.

## Evidence

Qualcomm describes QCA9565 as a combined WLAN/Bluetooth 4 solution; Dell G66T8
provides both driver functions and lists Inspiron 5567 support:
https://www.qualcomm.com/networking-infrastructure/products/qca9565
https://www.dell.com/support/home/en-us/drivers/driversdetails?driverid=g66t8

Linux's independent Bluetooth USB/firmware implementations are useful source
references, not macOS implementations or evidence of the notebook's USB ID:
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.12/drivers/bluetooth/ath3k.c
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.12/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c

## Local source references

The retained `src/linux/` reference tree already contains `ath3k.c`,
`btusb_main.c`, `btusb_qcom.c/.h`, `btqca.c/.h`, HCI headers, HCI event/core
handlers and LE advertising/EIR handling. Do not duplicate or replace these
files merely to reacquire them. Atheros USB bootstrap and the generic HCI
transport must both be integrated; PCI WLAN startup does not perform them.

Missing BLE security references `net/bluetooth/smp.c`, `ecdh_helper.c` and
`ecdh_helper.h` were downloaded from Linux v6.12, resolved to commit
`adc218676eef25575469234709c2d87185ca223a`. Their exact hashes, upstream URLs, licensing
and reference-only scope are recorded in `src/linux/linux-port-ledger.jsonl`.
The local reference tree remains intentionally excluded from Git. These Linux
files are research input, not linked macOS code or a completed Bluetooth path.
